# Roles & Permissions

## Portal roles (`user_profile.portal_role`)

| Role | Access |
|------|--------|
| `admin` | Full access (all flags treated as true) |
| `guest` | Sign in only; redirected to `/pending` |
| `member` | Access via department role matrix |

## Department roles (`access_role` + `user_department_role`)

Roles are **CRUD-managed** at `/roles` (Manager, HR, Viewer seeded by default). Access to `/users` and `/roles` is controlled by `navUsers` / `navRoles` plus the matching users/roles capability flags — **not** admin-only.

Each role defines permission flags (see `ACCESS_ROLE_PERMISSION_KEYS` in `src/lib/constants/access-role-permissions.ts`):

- **Nav:** `navDashboard`, `navEmployees`, `navDepartments`, `navFacilities`, `navPharmacy`, `navDoctors`, `navTools`, `navSettings`, `navCommunity`, `navUsers`, `navRoles`
- **Employees / doctors / pharmacy:** `*ReadAll`, `*Create`, `*Update`, `*Delete`, `*ExcelOverride` (where applicable)
- **Departments / facilities:** `*ReadAll`, `*Create`, `*Update`, `*Delete`
- **Users:** `usersRead`, `usersInvite`, `usersUpdate`, `usersInviteResend`, `usersInviteRevoke`. **Delete user** is portal **admin only** (not a role flag).
- **Roles:** `rolesRead`, `rolesCreate`, `rolesUpdate`, `rolesDelete`
- **Community:** `communityCategory*`, `communityLink*` Create/Update/Delete
- **Settings:** `settingsThemeUpdate`, plus newsletter/onboarding/announcement/sound/notification Create/Update/Delete
- **Tools manage:** `toolsService*`, `toolsApp*`, `toolsGuide*`, `toolsLearning*` Create/Update/Delete

There are **no** `*Write` columns — use Create and Update separately. Excel override is independent of Create/Update.

**Org scope:** `departmentUpdate` / `departmentDelete` and `facilityUpdate` / `facilityDelete` apply only to the user’s assigned department/facility rows. `departmentCreate` / `facilityCreate` are org-wide when the flag is set (not admin-only). `departmentReadAll` / `facilityReadAll` grant global read, not global update/delete.

Users get per-department assignments via `roleId` FK.

## Bootstrap

- First user (email or GitHub) → `admin`
- Later self-signups → `guest`
- Invited users → pre-assigned `admin` or `member` + department roles (not guest)

## Guards

- `requireUser` — authenticated
- `requireAppAccess` — not guest; has admin or ≥1 department role
- `requireAdmin` — portal admin only (rare; most pages use capability guards)
- `requireDashboardAccess` — `navDashboard` (or admin)
- `requireEmployeesAccess` — `navEmployees` + employee capability
- `requireDepartmentsAccess` — `navDepartments` + department capability
- `requireFacilitiesAccess` — `navFacilities` + facility capability
- `requirePharmacyAccess` — `navPharmacy` + pharmacy capability
- `requireDoctorsAccess` — `navDoctors` + doctor capability
- `requireToolsAccess` — `navTools` (or admin)
- `requireToolsManageAccess` — any `tools*` manage flag (or admin)
- `requireSettingsAccess` — `navSettings` (or admin)
- `requireUsersAccess` — `navUsers` + users capability (or admin)
- `requireRolesAccess` — `navRoles` + roles capability (or admin)
- `requireCommunityManage` — `navCommunity` (or admin). **Not** `navDashboard`.

Each private sidebar page has a matching layout/API guard. Nav flags control visibility/access; content CRUD uses the Create/Update/Delete/Excel (and users/roles/community/settings/tools) capability flags.

Services accept `UserPermissions` from `getUserPermissions(userId)`.

## Invites

- UI: `/users` → invite form → email with `/auth/accept-invite?token=…` (requires `usersInvite`)
- Single-use token, 24h expiry, resend/revoke from users UI (`usersInviteResend` / `usersInviteRevoke`)
- Accept: password only (name/roles pre-chosen)

